        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e1d175c4-16ab-5656-9bf8-fdc5ad587dcc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Winnie the Pooh (2011 film), Rudyard Kipling's The Jungle Book (1994 film)\n- People: Stephen Sommers, Edward S. Feldman, Raju Patel, Ronald Yanover, Mark Geldman, Travis Oates, Jim Cummings\n- Companies: Walt Disney Animation Studios, Walt Disney Pictures, Sisu Auto\n- Products: Nasu tracked articulated all-terrain transport vehicle\n- Organizations: Finnish Army\n\nFacts:\n- Rudyard Kipling's The Jungle Book is a 1994 live-action American adventure film.\n- Rudyard Kipling's The Jungle Book was co-written and directed by Stephen Sommers.\n- Rudyard Kipling's The Jungle Book was produced by Edward S. Feldman and Raju Patel from a story by Ronald Yanover and Mark Geldman.\n- Winnie the Pooh is a 2011 American animated buddy musical comedy film.\n- Winnie the Pooh was produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios and released by Walt Disney Pictures.\n- Travis Oates and Jim Cummings were the only two original voice actors to return for the 2011 Winnie the Pooh movie.\n- The Nasu is a tracked articulated all-terrain transport vehicle developed by Sisu Auto for the Finnish Army.\n- Nasu is an acronym for \"Nauha-Sisu\" and also means \"Piglet\" in Finnish.",
